# The archived record. Without this, GitHub's "Cite this repository" button produces an
# entry with no persistent identifier -- which is the one thing a citation is for.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20692282"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.20692282"
    description: "Archived record on Zenodo (concept DOI)"
abstract: >-
  KATAI 2D is a verification-first two-dimensional finite element engine for
  geotechnical engineering: staged construction, groundwater flow,
  consolidation, coupled flow-deformation, seismic dynamics and safety
  analysis over elastoplastic and creep constitutive models, driven from the
  command line or from Python. Every capability is validated against
  closed-form solutions, published benchmarks or independent computation
  paths, and the validation record ships with the source.
keywords:
  - geotechnical engineering
  - finite element method
  - soil mechanics
  - staged construction
  - consolidation
  - seepage
  - soil dynamics
  - slope stability
